pkg rest_english v1
  desc "English name-derived REST (List/Get/Create/Update/Delete → /api/…)"
  author "VEIL"

  # INV-001: verb prefixes are policy, not engine hardcodes.
  # Products that want different verbs or paths: use rest_rpc instead,
  # ship a forked pack, or override via veil.toml [codegen].
  http_name_policy
    list_prefix List
    get_prefix Get
    create_prefix Create
    update_prefix Update
    delete_prefix Delete
    path_prefix /api/

  prompt
    REST naming pack (rest_english) — migrate helper only after the flip:
    - New packages declare `endpoint` (method/path/handle). Do not write API `@route`.
    - `veil migrate harness` may still use these prefixes to seed endpoints.
    - `[harness] compat = "auto"` still synthesizes ListX → GET /api/{x}s, …
    - `[codegen] http_*` is unused by codegen when compat=off (warning).
    - Svelte page `@route("/path")` is unrelated and must never gain role:http_route.
